==============================================================================
  LorentzGATr Benchmark on QuarkGluon (bs=128)
  GPU: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB
  PyTorch: 2.10.0+cu128
  Data: /root/e2e/data/QuarkGluon/val.npz
  Each tier runs in a FRESH subprocess (no cross-contamination)
==============================================================================

  --- Part 1: Kernel-Level Microbenchmarks ---
  Shape: B=128, items=128, mv_channels=8, s_channels=16

  Kernel                         Baseline  Optimized  Speedup  BaseMem   OptMem
  ---------------------------- ---------- ---------- -------- -------- --------
  EquiLinear (fwd)                   459us       152us    3.03x      36MB      38MB
  Geometric Product (fwd)            305us       136us    2.25x     178MB      44MB
  Equi LayerNorm (fwd)               208us       261us    0.80x      44MB      36MB
  Gated GELU (fwd)                    34us       115us    0.29x      36MB      36MB

  --- Part 2: Model-Level Tiers ---


  Running 1. baseline (stock lgatr) ...
    infer=55.26ms  train=179.08ms  infer_mem=713MB  train_mem=5338MB

  Running 2. +kernels (fuse+GP) ...
    infer=35.61ms  train=110.35ms  infer_mem=733MB  train_mem=5311MB

  Running 3. +compile (with patches) ...
    infer=21.75ms  train=61.10ms  infer_mem=743MB  train_mem=3444MB

==============================================================================
  RESULTS
==============================================================================

  Tier                                Infer    Spd    IMem    Train    Spd    TMem
  -------------------------------- -------- ------ ------- -------- ------ -------
  1. baseline (stock lgatr)           55.3ms   1.0x    713MB   179.1ms   1.0x   5338MB
  2. +kernels (fuse+GP)               35.6ms   1.6x    733MB   110.3ms   1.6x   5311MB
  3. +compile (with patches)          21.8ms   2.5x    743MB    61.1ms   2.9x   3444MB

  Model: LorentzGATr, 708,992 params
  Config: 8 LGATr blocks (mv=8, s=16), num_classes=2
  Data: QuarkGluon val, 128 real jets, 128 particles, 4 features (pT, eta, phi, E)
  Isolation: each tier ran in a fresh Python subprocess

